2:[["$","div",null,{"className":"aeo-answer tl-dr","children":["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Quick Answer:"}]," A Bank PO 2026 study plan (SBI PO + IBPS PO) should span 5-7 months and cover five sections — Quantitative Aptitude, Reasoning, English, General/Banking Awareness, and Computer — for both Prelims and Mains. Speed is everything in banking exams (you get about 36 seconds per question). Study 5-6 hours daily, prioritizing Reasoning and Quant (highest weightage). Use an AI planner like PlanBot to schedule timed sectional practice, daily current affairs, and full-length mock series."]}]}],"\n",["$","h2",null,{"children":"Why Banking Exams Reward Speed Over Depth"}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"SBI PO and IBPS PO are the two biggest Probationary Officer recruitment exams in India — together selecting around 8,000-10,000 officers annually from over 20 lakh applicants."}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["Banking exams are ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"fundamentally different"}]," from academic exams. The syllabus isn't vast — Class 10 math, basic reasoning, school-level English. What's brutal is the ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"time pressure"}],": SBI PO Prelims gives you 60 minutes for 100 questions. That's ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"36 seconds per question"}],", including reading time."]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["This changes your entire strategy. You don't need to ",["$","em",null,{"children":"know"}]," advanced concepts. You need to ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"recognize patterns instantly and solve mechanically"}],". That comes from one thing: volume of timed practice."]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"An AI planner like PlanBot structures this volume practice so you're not wasting hours deciding what to study."}],"\n",["$","h2",null,{"children":"Understanding the Bank PO Exam Structure"}],"\n",["$","h3",null,{"children":"Prelims (Qualifying)"}],"\n",["$","table",null,{"children":[["$","thead",null,{"children":["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","th",null,{"children":"Section"}],["$","th",null,{"children":"Questions"}],["$","th",null,{"children":"Marks"}],["$","th",null,{"children":"Time"}]]}]}],["$","tbody",null,{"children":[["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","td",null,{"children":"English Language"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"30"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"30"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"20 min"}]]}],["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","td",null,{"children":"Quantitative Aptitude"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"35"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"35"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"20 min"}]]}],["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","td",null,{"children":"Reasoning Ability"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"35"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"35"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"20 min"}]]}]]}]]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Total:"}]," 100 questions · 100 marks · 60 minutes · Sectional timing · Negative marking 0.25"]}],"\n",["$","h3",null,{"children":"Mains (Merit-Deciding)"}],"\n",["$","table",null,{"children":[["$","thead",null,{"children":["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","th",null,{"children":"Section"}],["$","th",null,{"children":"Questions"}],["$","th",null,{"children":"Marks"}],["$","th",null,{"children":"Time"}]]}]}],["$","tbody",null,{"children":[["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","td",null,{"children":"Reasoning & Computer Aptitude"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"45"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"60"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"60 min"}]]}],["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","td",null,{"children":"Data Analysis & Interpretation"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"35"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"60"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"45 min"}]]}],["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","td",null,{"children":"General/Economy/Banking Awareness"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"40"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"40"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"35 min"}]]}],["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","td",null,{"children":"English Language"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"35"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"40"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"40 min"}]]}]]}]]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Total:"}]," 155 questions · 200 marks · 180 minutes · Followed by Descriptive Test (letter + essay, 30 min, 50 marks)"]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Then:"}]," Interview (for final merit)"]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Critical:"}]," Mains is much harder than Prelims. DI sets are complex, Reasoning puzzles are multi-layered, and GA is unpredictable. Plan for Mains from day one."]}],"\n",["$","h2",null,{"children":"The 6-Month Bank PO Master Plan"}],"\n",["$","h3",null,{"children":"Phase 1: Fundamentals + Prelims Focus (Months 1-3)"}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Objective:"}]," Build concept clarity and Prelims-level speed"]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Daily Study Target:"}]," 5-6 hours"]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["$","strong",null,{"children":"Section Split:"}]}],"\n",["$","ul",null,{"children":["\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Quant: 1.5-2 hours/day"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Reasoning: 1.5 hours/day"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"English: 1 hour/day"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"General/Banking Awareness: 45-60 min/day (foundation only)"}],"\n"]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["$","strong",null,{"children":"Section-Wise Strategy:"}]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["$","strong",null,{"children":"Quantitative Aptitude:"}]}],"\n",["$","ul",null,{"children":["\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Fundamentals: Simplification, Number Series, Quadratic Equations (these are 10-15 free marks)"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Arithmetic: Percentages, Ratio, Profit-Loss, Time-Speed, SI/CI, Averages (50% of quant)"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"DI: Tables, Bar, Line, Pie (start here in month 2)"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Target: 200+ questions daily by month 2"}],"\n"]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["$","strong",null,{"children":"Reasoning:"}]}],"\n",["$","ul",null,{"children":["\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Puzzles & Seating Arrangement: 60% of reasoning — practice 2-3 puzzles daily"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Syllogism, Inequality, Coding-Decoding: 15-min daily drill"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Blood Relations, Direction, Order-Ranking: easy marks, don't neglect"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Target: 100+ questions daily by month 2"}],"\n"]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["$","strong",null,{"children":"English:"}]}],"\n",["$","ul",null,{"children":["\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Reading Comprehension: 2-3 passages daily (this is 30-40% of English)"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Grammar: Error detection, Sentence Improvement, Cloze Test"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Vocab: 30 words daily (especially banking/finance terms)"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Target: daily reading habit is non-negotiable"}],"\n"]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["$","strong",null,{"children":"General Awareness:"}]}],"\n",["$","ul",null,{"children":["\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Start Banking Awareness (RBI, types of accounts, banking terms)"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Daily 30 min current affairs"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Don't go deep yet — build foundation"}],"\n"]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"How PlanBot Helps:"}]," ",["$","em",null,{"children":"\"Bank PO 2026, both SBI and IBPS. Can study 6 hours daily. Weak in puzzles and DI.\""}]," PlanBot schedules extra puzzle and DI sets in your peak focus hours and builds timed practice blocks."]}],"\n",["$","h3",null,{"children":"Phase 2: Speed Building + Sectional Mastery (Months 4-5)"}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Objective:"}]," Hit Prelims speed targets + start Mains prep"]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Daily Study Target:"}]," 6 hours"]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["$","strong",null,{"children":"What Changes:"}]}],"\n",["$","ul",null,{"children":["\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Timed sectional practice"}]," becomes the core activity"]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Start Mains-level DI and Reasoning"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Full-length Prelims mocks (3-4 per week)"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Banking Awareness goes deeper"}],"\n"]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["$","strong",null,{"children":"Speed Targets (Prelims):"}]}],"\n",["$","ul",null,{"children":["\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Quant: 30+ correct in 20 min (need to attempt smartly, skip hard)"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Reasoning: 28+ correct in 20 min"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"English: 25+ correct in 20 min"}],"\n"]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"The Art of Skippage:"}]," Banking exams reward knowing what to ",["$","em",null,{"children":"skip"}],". A puzzle that takes 5 minutes for 5 marks is a trap. Practice identifying and skipping time-sinks. This is where most aspirants fail."]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"How PlanBot Helps:"}]," ",["$","em",null,{"children":"\"Prelims score stuck at 65/100. Time runs out in Quant.\""}]," PlanBot reallocates to Quant speed drills and DI shortcuts for two weeks."]}],"\n",["$","h3",null,{"children":"Phase 3: Mains Mastery + Mock Series (Month 6)"}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Objective:"}]," Mains-level preparation + full mock series + Descriptive prep"]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Daily Study Target:"}]," 6-7 hours"]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["$","strong",null,{"children":"What Changes:"}]}],"\n",["$","ul",null,{"children":["\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Full-length Mains mocks (2-3 per week)"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Complex DI sets (caselets, missing data, arithmetic-based)"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Advanced puzzles (floor, scheduling, multi-variable)"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Descriptive Test prep: write 1 letter + 1 essay daily"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"GA: last 4 months current affairs revision + Banking Awareness"}],"\n"]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["$","strong",null,{"children":"Descriptive Test Tips:"}]}],"\n",["$","ul",null,{"children":["\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Format matters (formal letter structure)"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Practice on a keyboard — typing speed is critical (30 min for 2 pieces)"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Read model essays to build structure"}],"\n"]}],"\n",["$","h2",null,{"children":"How to Use PlanBot for Bank PO — A Practical Workflow"}],"\n",["$","ol",null,{"children":["\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Set both exam goals:"}]," Tell PlanBot you're preparing for both SBI PO and IBPS PO (different dates). The AI syncs a unified plan around both."]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Practice-first scheduling:"}]," ",["$","em",null,{"children":"\"3 hours of timed practice daily + 2 hours concept revision.\""}]," PlanBot blocks timed practice sets with built-in review windows."]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Current affairs continuity:"}]," PlanBot schedules a fixed daily GA block so you never fall behind — critical for banking awareness."]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Streaks for consistency:"}]," Bank PO prep is 6 months of daily practice. Streaks keep you accountable when motivation dips in month 4."]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Weekly AI report (Elite+):"}]," See your actual time distribution. If you spent 40% on Quant but Quant is your strength, reallocate."]}],"\n"]}],"\n",["$","h2",null,{"children":"Common Bank PO Mistakes That Cost Selection"}],"\n",["$","ul",null,{"children":["\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Treating Prelims and Mains as the same exam"}]," — Mains difficulty is 2x; prepare accordingly"]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Not practicing skippage"}]," — trying to attempt every question kills your score"]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Ignoring the Descriptive Test"}]," — qualifying, but many strong candidates fail it"]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"GA cramming"}]," — banking awareness takes 3-4 months of daily effort"]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"No timed practice"}]," — solving 50 questions in an hour ≠ solving 50 in 20 minutes"]}],"\n"]}],"\n",["$","h2",null,{"children":"Frequently Asked Questions"}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Can I prepare for SBI PO and IBPS PO simultaneously?"}]," Yes — syllabus is 95% identical. Prepare once, write both. IBPS typically follows SBI by 2-3 months."]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Is Bank PO harder than SSC CGL?"}]," Different. SSC is syllabus-deep; Bank PO is speed-focused. Bank PO Quant is easier, but time pressure is intense."]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"How fast should my typing be for the Descriptive Test?"}]," Aim for 30-35 WPM minimum. You need to write ~400 words (essay) and ~150 words (letter) in 30 minutes."]}],"\n",["$","h2",null,{"children":"Start Your Bank PO 2026 Prep Today"}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"Banking exams are the most predictable competitive exams in India — the question types repeat, and speed beats depth. With 6 months of structured daily practice, selection is very achievable."}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","a",null,{"href":"https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=cpm.planbot","children":"Get PlanBot free on Android"}]," and let the AI build your Bank PO 2026 study schedule."]}]]
